The trouble is, Windows closes DOS windows automatically when they are
done. You can either run NH manually from the command prompt
(Start->All Programs->Accessories->Command Prompt or Start->Run and
type "cmd") or 

change the command line of your shortcut to something like 

cmd /k "C:\NetHack\NetHack.exe"

The "cmd" runs the command prompt window; the /k tells it to run the
command entered immediately following and keep the window open.

